From f8a72dd865b1a33fc5c3c856c9fee8bb130466d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:45:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223A: fog and lamp light at reduced resolution
 (hdFogResolution, hdLightPassResolution; default half)

- Fog: march and horizontal blur on scatter images at 1/2 or 1/4; the composite does the vertical blur and a
  depth-aware upsample (two nearest columns x 9 rows, depth similarity, plain-blend fallback); fog status text copied
  (it kept the first message's pointer)
- Lamp light: LIGHT_PASS 1 lights 1/scale pixels into an RGBA16F image (rgb + view depth, tiles of 16 low pixels),
  LIGHT_PASS 2 applies per screen pixel from the 4 nearest by depth with its own normal; debug views stay full
- Shader generators: fog/gen_fog_spv.py (new), shader-work/lights_spv.py (three variants)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
